      ],
      "id": "f8d6970d-2a46-4476-b8c3-8c484b874e8a",
      "name": "Fetch Invoice PDF"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "binary",
        "responseDataSource": "set",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [
        1248,
        -96
      ],
      "id": "e4489605-11a8-492b-a6c0-70a6f83b4dd4",
      "name": "Respond to Webhook"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Serve Invoice PDFs\nBuilt: 2026-07-08 | Revised: 2026-10-07 (retest pending) | Stateless webhook, no file storage\n\nTwilio's WhatsApp API fetches media from a URL rather than accepting attachments directly. This workflow answers that fetch: it re-authenticates to Odoo and re-renders the requested invoice fresh, every call.\n\n**Access control:** the URL must carry `invoice_id`, `exp` (unix seconds) and `token` = HMAC-SHA256(\"invoice_id.exp\", PDF_LINK_SECRET). Anything else - bad id format, expired link, wrong token - gets a 403 and never reaches Odoo. The main workflow signs the links.\n\nMust be toggled **Active** (not just open) for the webhook to respond.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 1600
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -304,
        -480
      ],
      "id": "9380696f-6631-4e85-b3b1-63d3d042a4eb",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Note on Odoo auth\nThis uses session-cookie auth (web login), NOT the same as the uid/JSON-RPC auth used in the main workflow's search_read calls. Odoo genuinely has two separate auth systems - this one is required specifically for the PDF report engine.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 420,
        "color": "#FBDC0E"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        144,
        304
      ],
      "id": "8c6b292f-614b-4938-8fd5-0314e24d068a",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    }
  ],
